# Flash feedback — FlashGrowl only

All **session flash** feedback (success, error, info, warning) is shown **globally** via:

- `FlashGrowl` component (layout-level)
- `useGrowl` composable (Metronic `KTToast`)

## Do

- Set flash in Laravel: `redirect()->with('success', '...')` or shared keys consumed by `HandleInertiaRequests`
- Read flash in the layout / `FlashGrowl` and fire toasts with `useGrowl`
- Use consistent flash keys the app already defines (do not invent per-page keys without reason)

## Do not

- Render inline flash banners, alert boxes, or `<div v-if="flash">` blocks inside individual pages
- Duplicate toast logic in page components when the global handler can show it once

## New pages

When adding Inertia pages, assume flash is already handled at the layout level. Do not add page-local success/error markup for session messages.
